## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design scalable, multi-tenant data pipelines that handle schema diversity, guarantee data quality, and maintain operational reliability under high throughput.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant schema registry and validation
- Idempotent upserts using Iceberg MERGE operations
- Late data handling with time-partitioned snapshots
- Data quality enforcement via JSON Schema and Great Expectations
- Observability through comprehensive monitoring and automated rollback testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function upsertEvent(table, event) {
  // Validate against tenant-specific schema
  const isValid = validateEvent(event.tenant_id, event);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Schema validation failed');

  // Perform idempotent upsert using MERGE
  return table.merge()
    .whenMatched().updateAll()
    .whenNotMatched().insertAll()
    .execute();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable data lifecycle with multi-tenant governance and cost control; integrates Iceberg features, storage tiering, policy-driven retention, and query-layer masking.

## Key Concepts
- Iceberg time travel via snapshots
- Dynamic data tiering (hot/warm/cold)
- Per-tenant data masking
- Encryption at rest (KMS)
- Partition pruning and metadata caching

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectTier(tenant, ageDays) {
  const retention = (tenantRetention[tenant] || 365);
  if (ageDays < 30) return 'hot';
  if (ageDays < retention) return 'warm';
  return 'cold';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test data freshness and mask correctness across tiers?
- How would you validate time travel remains accurate after tiering moves?
